-- title:
--   Node depth along the substitution degeneracy leg at ℓ≠ q
-- statement:
--   Fix $N\ge 1$ and a prime $q$ with $q\nmid N$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that the image of $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; then $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ has characteristic $q$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,N$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces q N k`; let `data` be modular polynomial data at $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence $\Phi \bmod q=(C X^{q}-X)(C X-X^{q})$; assume the two level-$q$ degeneracy maps $\bar\alpha,\bar\beta$ from level $N$ to level $Nq$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ are integral; and fix a `PlaceSpecialization` $P$ at $A$, a prolongation tuple $R$ over it satisfying `IsModel`, `OrderLawFixed`, `RegularityLaw W` and `NodeValueLaw W`, together with, at each $w\in W$, a number field $K_w\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, node coordinates $c_w=(x_w,y_w)$ over $K_w$ at $w$, an element $\varpi_w$ of $A\cap K_w$ generating the kernel of the reduction on $A\cap K_w$, the value-integrality law at $w$, and a crossing presentation $x_wy_w=\mathrm{nodeConst}(\varpi_w)^{E}u$ with $E\ge1$ and $u$ a unit of the node ring. Let $\ell\neq q$ be a prime and fix the analogous package $(W_r,\bar\alpha_r,\bar\beta_r,P_r,R_r,\dots)$ at level $N\ell$, summarised here in the same way. Assume the substitution map $\mathrm{towerSubstBar}$ from level $Nq$ to level $N\ell q$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is integral, that $\mathrm{heckeBetaC}\,k\,N\,\ell$ into the roof $\mathrm{charLDegeneracyRoof}\,k\,N\,\ell$ is integral, and that $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,(N\ell)$ is contained in that roof by an integral inclusion. Let $y_1$ be a place of the roof restricting to $y\in W_r$ along the inclusion and to $w\in W$ along $\mathrm{heckeBetaC}$. Then for every place $V'$ of the level-$N\ell q$ field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $P_r.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V'=y$ and with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}$ of the restriction $V'|$ along $\mathrm{towerSubstBar}$ equal to $w$, the depth $(c_w).\mathrm{yDepth}(V'|)$, namely the $A$-valuation of the value of $y_w$ at $V'|$, equals $(c_{r,y}).\mathrm{yDepth}(V')$ raised to the ramification index of $y_1$ along $\mathrm{heckeBetaC}$ in the value group of $A$, and $P.\mathrm{IsStrictFst}(V'|)$ holds if and only if $P_r.\mathrm{IsStrictFst}(V')$ does.
--
--   This is the transfer of node depths and of the strictness condition from level $N\ell$ down to level $N$ along the substitution leg of the degeneracy tower at a prime $\ell$ different from the residue characteristic $q$, the two levels being compared through a common place of the roof field generated by the relevant $j$-expansions. It is used in the level-raising step that produces a place over $A$ with prescribed depth behaviour along the inclusion degeneracy map $\bar\alpha$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_PlaceSpecialization_yDepth_restrictAlong_towerSubstBar_eq_yDepth_pow_ramificationIndexAlong_heckeBetaC_of_prime.lean

